    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d402">

                <pb facs="0569" n="463" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg463"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Chargé Sleeper.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-08-31"><hi rendition="#italic">August 31,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 59.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 160, of the 25th instant, reporting further in regard to the insurrection in
                    Cuba.</p>
                <p>The department approves without reservation the energetic activity and wise
                    foresight displayed in your recent communication to the <pb facs="0570" n="464"
                        xml:id="pg464"/> Cuban Government. The department desires you to call the
                    attention of the Cuban Government to any and every injury to American interests
                    in Cuba and to urge the Government to accord that protection without which
                    American interests must be jeopardized.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
